@* Purpose: Renders the Enterprise Governance UI and coordinates its pages interactions. *@
@page "/admin/enterprise-governance"
@using System.Net.Http.Json
@using Dip.Domain.Entities
@inject HttpClient Http
<PageTitle>Enterprise Governance | DIP</PageTitle>
<section class="page-heading"><div><div class="eyebrow">Enterprise administration</div><h1>Governance & integrity</h1><p>Tenant boundaries, identity resolution, evidence integrity and retention controls.</p></div><div class="heading-actions"><a class="btn btn-outline-secondary" href="/admin/fleet">Agent fleet</a></div></section>
<div class="row g-3">
<div class="col-md-6">
<div class="card h-100">
<div class="card-body">
<h5>Tamper-evident evidence</h5>
<p>Phase 5 stores payload hash, previous hash, chain hash and optional device signature for each integrity receipt.</p>
<p class="text-muted">Verification never changes the source evidence; it only reports Verified / Unsigned / InvalidSignature / BrokenChain.</p></div></div></div>
<div class="col-md-6">
<div class="card h-100">
<div class="card-body">
<h5>Privacy boundary</h5>
<p>Existing Phase 1 policy remains authoritative for screenshot/video/raw artifact collection. Endpoint agents are limited to configured project roots and allowed production tools.</p>
<p class="text-muted">No keylogging, password capture or hidden personal-folder monitoring is enabled.</p></div></div></div>
<div class="col-md-6">
<div class="card h-100">
<div class="card-body">
<h5>Cross-source identity</h5>
<p>GitHub, Windows, Maya and other identities are mapped to an IdentityProfile. Low-confidence links require administrator approval rather than silent auto-merge.</p></div></div></div>
<div class="col-md-6">
<div class="card h-100">
<div class="card-body">
<h5>Retention</h5>
<p>Metadata, artifact and video retention values continue to come from effective policy. Execution is audited through retention execution records.</p></div></div></div></div>
